{"meta":{"ticker":"FIW","as_of_date":"2026-08-07","performance_as_of":"2026-07-31","generated_at":"2026-08-09 18:16:12"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"FIW","fund_name":"First Trust Water ETF","category":"US Thematic","issuer":"First Trust","index_name":"ISE Clean Edge Water Index","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.005,"aum":1935152513,"holdings_count":38,"inception_date":"2007-05-08","overall_score":2.34610044169611,"overall_rank":977,"sector_diversification_score":4.37176291793313},"description":{"tsi_description":"FIW is a thematic water infrastructure ETF that tracks the ISE Clean Edge Water Index and invests in companies involved in potable water, wastewater, and related water technologies. The fund uses a modified market-cap-weighting approach that balances exposure across larger and smaller water-related companies while maintaining relatively low portfolio turnover. Unlike broader industrial or utility ETFs, FIW provides concentrated exposure to the water industry across multiple sectors, including Industrials, Utilities, Health Care, and Technology. The strategy also maintains meaningful exposure to small- and mid-cap companies, contributing to a differentiated risk and return profile relative to the broader market. Overall, FIW offers targeted exposure to the global water industry through a rules-based indexing framework.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the ISE Clean Edge Water Index.","Invests in companies deriving substantial revenue from potable water, wastewater, and related water industries.","Requires minimum market capitalization, liquidity, float, and trading history thresholds for eligibility.","Selects the top 36 eligible securities by market capitalization.","Uses a modified market-cap-weighting methodology with tiered weight assignments based on company size ranking.","Assigns fixed weight ranges across different market-cap tiers within the portfolio.","Rec